@startuml sequence_pipelined_event_batching
!include ../../../design/theme.iuml

title Pipelined Command Execution with Batched Event Delivery

actor Client
participant "Server Connection" as Conn
participant "runBatch" as Batch
participant "Pipeline" as Pipeline
participant "Event Bus" as EventBus
participant "Plugin Event Queue" as Queue
participant "GCPC Writer" as Writer
participant "IPC Plugin SDK" as SDK
participant "Instrumentation Plugin" as Instr

Client -> Conn : command A\ncommand B\ncommand C (pipelined)
Conn -> Batch : collect available commands

Batch -> Pipeline : EvaluatePreLocked(A)
Pipeline -> EventBus : operation.started(A)
Pipeline --> Conn : result A
Pipeline -> EventBus : operation.completed(A)
EventBus -> Queue : enqueue events A

Batch -> Pipeline : EvaluatePreLocked(B)
Pipeline -> EventBus : operation.started(B)
Pipeline --> Conn : result B
Pipeline -> EventBus : operation.completed(B)
EventBus -> Queue : enqueue events B

Batch -> Pipeline : EvaluatePreLocked(C)
Pipeline -> EventBus : operation.started(C)
Pipeline --> Conn : result C
Pipeline -> EventBus : operation.completed(C)
EventBus -> Queue : enqueue events C
Conn --> Client : ordered replies A, B, C

Queue -> Writer : flush event batch [A,B,C]
Writer -> SDK : GCPC EventV1 frames\n(or compatible batch path)
SDK -> Instr : dispatch operation events

note over Conn,Pipeline
RESP pipelining remains N commands with N ordered replies.
Event batching is transport-only and observational.
end note

note over Queue,Writer
Batch limits: max count, max bytes, max delay.
Overflow/gaps must be visible.
end note

@enduml
